{
  "id": "spreading-activation",
  "term": "spreading activation",
  "definition": "Spreading activation is the idea that memory works like an associative network, so activating one cue can trigger related information and help bring a personally experienced event to mind. In this context, it refers to recall benefiting when a self-generated cue sets off connected memories.",
